      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I guess I didn't really explain another concept:\n\nIf someone were to set that number to 5, 10, or the max of 128, it means that avatars get *that many more steps* lower quality, multiplied by however many textures there are in that world. So this really has a significant opportunity for unintentional abuse.\n\nI think a compromise could be to only allow \"0 or 1\" as values so people can still use the priority for artistic intent. But otherwise, I see no point in allowing people to change the priority of textures.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
