      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f80c1df30fd4366bc64383e|full_name} This shouldn't be a notable issue. Mipmap streaming already prioritizes closer textures. The entire point is to just *unload* mipmaps that are not being used. Mipmap are generally enabled across the board already, so you should almost literally *not* see a degradation of quality. \n\nIf anything, users will actually be able to enjoy your world instead of the alternative, which would be crashing or poor performance. And users with appropriate VRAM (10, 12, 16, 24, etc.) will just get a better quality experience.\n\nI do not know where this boogeyman idea came from. You are the second person I've seen who had this concern.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
